    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by **Yordan Alvarez**, who claims our highest efficiency score of 71.62. His elite 0.452 xwOBA remains the cornerstone of our offensive strategy, effectively neutralizing the standard park penalties. We are also projecting significant upside from our leadoff hitters; **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (63.14) and **Lars Nootbaar** (65.16) benefit from prime lineup positioning and favorable dynamic platoon advantages against their respective right-handed matchups. **Trea Turner** (66.93) remains an automatic start, as his ability to impact the SB category\u2014our primary scarcity target\u2014combined with his promotion to the #2 spot, makes him essential even against a serviceable arm in Clarke. \n\nThe primary lineup tension today centered on **Junior Caminero** (49.84), who narrowly edged out a potential start from **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**. While **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** possesses high theoretical pop, his current bench status and the optimizer\u2019s preference for **Junior Caminero**\u2019s consistent plate appearances in the #3 hole dictated the final decision. Conversely, we are proceeding with caution regarding **Carson Benge** (45.29); his score is suppressed significantly by the daunting 3.51 xERA of Jax, a matchup that forces us to prioritize floor over ceiling. We continue to monitor the status of **Casey Schmitt**, who remains sidelined, while **Christian Yelich**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Josh Smith**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** are held in reserve. While **Colt Keith** (58.19) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (60.51) offer strong value, we are cognizant of the risks posed by Misiorowski\u2019s elite stuff against **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, which serves as our most volatile situational flag on the board today.",
